    {
      "id": "surface-boundary",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive",
      "position": {
        "x": 1150,
        "y": 500
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive",
        "body": "- Surface does not replace faces, Content, or Glyph. It orders and scopes them; it doesn't render in their place.\n- Surface is not an export. A Surface is about which *faces* a graph offers to a host; an export is about which *classes or resources* a graph offers an importer. They used to share the `root.surfaces[]` array; presentation Surfaces are now edges, and that array is the exposed entries (`port`, `export` and `view`).",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592079328,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
